---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
---
<Base
  title={`Editorial policy & disclaimer | ${site.name}`}
  description="What this site is, what it is not, and how it is funded."
  path="/disclaimer/"
>
  <div class="article-page">
    <Header />
    <main class="static-main">
      <p class="static-eyebrow">Editorial policy</p>
      <h1>Editorial policy &amp; disclaimer</h1>

      <h2>Not tax advice</h2>
      <p>
        Everything on {site.name} is general information about U.S. federal tax
        rules. It is not tax, legal, accounting or financial advice, and it is not
        a substitute for advice from a licensed professional who knows your facts.
        Reading this site, subscribing to the newsletter or contacting us does not
        create a client relationship of any kind.
      </p>
      <p>
        The author is not a Certified Public Accountant, an enrolled agent or a tax
        attorney, is not licensed to practice before the IRS, and does not prepare
        or review returns. Before acting on anything you read here, check the cited
        sources and consider consulting a licensed tax professional.
      </p>

      <h2>Federal rules only</h2>
      <p>
        Unless a column says otherwise, it describes federal rules. State and local
        tax law differs, sometimes sharply, and a federal answer can be the wrong
        answer in your state.
      </p>

      <h2>Accuracy and dates</h2>
      <p>
        Tax rules change every year, and mid-year changes happen. Year-specific
        columns carry the tax year they describe and the date the rules were last
        checked. If a cited source has changed since that date, the source governs,
        not this site. Report an error and it will be corrected on the page with an
        updated review date.
      </p>

      <h2>Sources</h2>
      <p>
        Columns cite primary sources — IRS publications and form instructions, the
        Internal Revenue Code, and Treasury regulations. Secondary commentary is
        used only where it is labeled as such. Links to sources open externally and
        are not paid placements.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising and affiliate disclosure</h2>
      <p>
        This site is funded by display advertising and affiliate links. When you
        buy through an affiliate link, {site.name} may earn a commission at no
        additional cost to you. Affiliate relationships never determine what a
        column says, which rule is described, or which product is recommended.
        Columns that contain affiliate links say so on the page.
      </p>

      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The content is provided "as is," without warranty of any kind. To the
        fullest extent permitted by law, {site.name} and its author are not liable
        for any loss arising from reliance on this site, including penalties,
        interest or additional tax.
      </p>

      <h2>IRS Circular 230 notice</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing on this site is a covered opinion or written tax advice within the
        meaning of Treasury Department Circular 230, and nothing here may be used
        to avoid tax penalties.
      </p>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </div>
</Base>
